## Summary

The largest issue cluster in the repo is kernel work falling between the
cracks of an implicit contract: job output that never reaches the caller,
processes that outlive their jobs, sessions wedged by a blocking call,
result surfaces that differ between call sites. The Elixir cutover
(supervised per-cell processes) fixed the substrate. This plan finishes the
job: one lifecycle every kernel operation follows, one result type every
caller reads, and no way to spawn work outside it.

<Dag
  nodes={[
